---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Work – Gabriel Alisasis"
  description="Four production builds, real GoHighLevel and Zapier workflow samples, work history, and selected projects from CRM automation through to machine learning."
>
  <div class="page-top-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <section id="client-work">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="sec-num">01</span>
        <div>
          <span class="sec-kicker">Client work</span>
          <h2>Four builds, live in production</h2>
          <p>The engagements I'd point to first. Each one opens into the full record – what was broken, how I diagnosed it, and what shipped.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="case-list">
        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-top">
            <div class="case-shot">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">cordeliaarc.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Cordelia ARC homepage showing the headline Compassionate Care for Brighter Futures over a photo of a caregiver with a client">
            </div>
            <div class="case-info">
              <div class="case-idx">Case 01 / 04</div>
              <h3>Cordelia ARC – supportive-living platform, public site to admin back office</h3>
              <p>A California supportive-living agency serving adults with intellectual disabilities across Alameda and Contra Costa counties. What began as a marketing site became the software the agency runs on – referrals, hiring, compliance, and billing.</p>
              <blockquote class="pullquote">The same referral and intake operations I usually automate inside a CRM – this time built as an actual application.</blockquote>
              <dl class="spec">
                <div><dt>Sector</dt><dd>Healthcare · HIPAA-regulated</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>React · TypeScript · Supabase</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>91 migrations · ~50 edge functions</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Surface</dt><dd>40+ routed pages</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="case-actions">
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://cordeliaarc.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit site ↗</a>
              <a class="visit-btn" href="/work/cordelia-arc">Read the case study →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-top">
            <div class="case-shot">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">kempbeauty.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Kemp Beauty homepage hero reading Imagine waking up with perfect lashes over a close-up beauty photograph">
            </div>
            <div class="case-info">
              <div class="case-idx">Case 02 / 04</div>
              <h3>Kemp Beauty – the email problem nobody could see</h3>
              <p>A DTC lash brand with eight live Klaviyo flows and a storefront that needed real product-page work. The flows all showed green in the dashboard. Almost none of the email was reaching anyone.</p>
              <blockquote class="pullquote">All eight flows showed live. None of them were being delivered.</blockquote>
              <dl class="spec">
                <div><dt>Sector</dt><dd>DTC beauty · Shopify</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Deliverability · theme dev</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Fixed</dt><dd>26 messages across 8 flows</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Root cause</dt><dd>DMARC p=reject, unsigned domain</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="case-actions">
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://kempbeauty.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit store ↗</a>
              <a class="visit-btn" href="/work/kemp-beauty">Read the case study →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-top">
            <div class="case-shot">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">sellready.ai</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Sell Ready AI homepage with the headline Scale Beyond Bottlenecks and a website-input call to action over a blue gradient">
            </div>
            <div class="case-info">
              <div class="case-idx">Case 03 / 04</div>
              <h3>Sell Ready AI – 23 landing pages and a podcast platform, inside Shopify</h3>
              <p>An AI-systems consultancy whose Shopify theme had to behave like a full marketing site: two dozen service and resource pages, a searchable podcast archive, and a video-led homepage – all in Liquid.</p>
              <blockquote class="pullquote">Shopify gives you a storefront. Everything that makes this feel like a content platform had to be built.</blockquote>
              <dl class="spec">
                <div><dt>Sector</dt><dd>B2B consultancy</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>Shopify Liquid · JS · CSS</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>87 sections · 23 templates</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Built</dt><dd>Podcast archive, search, tags</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="case-actions">
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://sellready.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit site ↗</a>
              <a class="visit-btn" href="/work/sell-ready-ai">Read the case study →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-top">
            <div class="case-shot">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">shop.orangeashes.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="649" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Orange Ashes storefront homepage, a digital product shop styled in clay orange, amber and cream">
            </div>
            <div class="case-info">
              <div class="case-idx">Case 04 / 04</div>
              <h3>Orange Ashes – a digital product store built inside GoHighLevel</h3>
              <p>A digital product shop serving Pampered Chef consultants, built and maintained end to end in GoHighLevel – store, checkout, fulfilment, branded email, and a hand-coded front-end layer on top.</p>
              <blockquote class="pullquote">GoHighLevel wasn't designed to be a storefront. Making it behave like one meant overriding it where it pushed back.</blockquote>
              <dl class="spec">
                <div><dt>Sector</dt><dd>Digital products · e-commerce</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>GoHighLevel · HTML/CSS/JS</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Catalogue</dt><dd>9 collections · 24 products</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Email</dt><dd>Mailgun-authenticated domain</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="case-actions">
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://shop.orangeashes.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit store ↗</a>
              <a class="visit-btn" href="/work/orange-ashes">Read the case study →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="workflows">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="sec-num">02</span>
        <div>
          <span class="sec-kicker">Workflow samples</span>
          <h2>Inside the automations</h2>
          <p>Real builds pulled straight from GoHighLevel and Zapier – the actual trigger, the logic branching, and where the data ends up. Click any screenshot to enlarge.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="wf-list">
        <div class="wf-card reveal">
          <div class="wf-shot">
            <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="633" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                 alt="GoHighLevel workflow builder showing the EDC time-slot form submission trigger branching into contact-tag actions">
          </div>
          <div class="wf-info">
            <div class="wf-meta"><span class="n mono">01 / 04</span><span class="tag tag-trigger">GoHighLevel</span></div>
            <h3>EDC time-slot form → shuttle &amp; hotel routing → Google Sheets</h3>
            <p>Guests submit a form with their arrival time slot. The workflow triggers on submission, tags the contact, then checks the notes field to work out which shuttle and hotel package applies – and writes the result into the ops Google Sheet so the ground team has it without asking.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wf-card reveal">
          <div class="wf-shot">
            <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="674" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                 alt="Zapier multi-step zap fanning a new event booking out into six venue-specific paths">
          </div>
          <div class="wf-info">
            <div class="wf-meta"><span class="n mono">02 / 04</span><span class="tag tag-action">Zapier</span></div>
            <h3>Multi-venue event booking → GoHighLevel contact sync</h3>
            <p>A new booking arrives from the events calendar and immediately splits into six paths – one per venue across the Vegas and Miami locations. Each path creates or updates the right contact in GoHighLevel with venue-specific tags, so reporting stays clean per property.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wf-card reveal">
          <div class="wf-shot">
            <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="677" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                 alt="Zapier workflow splitting a WooCommerce order into shuttle and hotel opportunity paths">
          </div>
          <div class="wf-info">
            <div class="wf-meta"><span class="n mono">03 / 04</span><span class="tag tag-action">Zapier</span></div>
            <h3>WooCommerce order → shuttle or hotel opportunity</h3>
            <p>Fires the moment a customer buys a shuttle or hotel package on WooCommerce. The order splits into two paths based on what was purchased, and each one opens the matching opportunity in the CRM pipeline – so sales sees the deal without anyone re-entering it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wf-card reveal">
          <div class="wf-shot">
            <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="677" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                 alt="Zapier workflow monitoring a Gmail inbox and routing affiliate emails through an AI step into the CRM">
          </div>
          <div class="wf-info">
            <div class="wf-meta"><span class="n mono">04 / 04</span><span class="tag tag-trigger">Zapier + AI</span></div>
            <h3>Inbox monitoring → AI affiliate detection → CRM update</h3>
            <p>Watches a Gmail inbox and splits incoming mail on whether the subject line mentions an affiliate. Affiliate email gets passed to an AI step that reads the message and extracts the details, which then update the contact record in the CRM automatically.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="experience">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="sec-num">03</span>
        <div>
          <span class="sec-kicker">Experience</span>
          <h2>Work history</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="xp">
        <div class="reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="xp-when">Mar 2025 – Jun 2026</span>
            <span class="xp-where">LiveHowYouWantUSA<br>United States</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Operations Support Analyst</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Managed <strong>GoHighLevel CRM</strong>, workflows, forms, automations, and daily operational processes.</li>
              <li>Maintained Bubble backend workflows and customer data for seamless platform performance.</li>
              <li>Built and managed online communities that scaled from <strong>900 to 36,000+ members in 8 months</strong>.</li>
              <li>Resolved operational issues while improving customer experience and internal efficiency.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="site-preview">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">livehowyouwant.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable site-shot" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="760" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Live How You Want homepage – the CRM and community platform">
              <div class="site-body">
                <span>CRM &amp; community platform I helped run</span>
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://livehowyouwant.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="xp-when">Oct 2024 – Aug 2025</span>
            <span class="xp-where">Supreme Club Tours<br>United States</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Marketing Automation Specialist</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Built GoHighLevel automations for lead capture, nurturing, and customer communication.</li>
              <li>Managed CRM operations supporting growth to <strong>3,000+ customers within 5 months</strong>.</li>
              <li>Managed partnerships with brands including Insomniac, supporting audience growth and bookings.</li>
              <li>Designed marketing assets and promotional materials for Las Vegas nightlife campaigns.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="site-preview">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">supremeclubtours.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable site-shot" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Supreme Club Tours homepage – Las Vegas nightlife and events booking site">
              <div class="site-body">
                <span>Las Vegas nightlife &amp; events site I supported</span>
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://supremeclubtours.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="xp-when">Apr 2023 – Sep 2023</span>
            <span class="xp-where">BSU STEER HUB<br>Philippines</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Front-End Developer</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Developed and tested real-time web application features.</li>
              <li>Improved user interface functionality and usability.</li>
              <li>Maintained responsive front-end components and system performance.</li>
              <li>Used performance analytics to optimize content strategy and engagement.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="site-preview">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">steerhub.batstateu.edu.ph</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable site-shot" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="676" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="BSU STEER HUB homepage – the university web application I helped develop">
              <div class="site-body">
                <span>University web app I helped develop</span>
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://steerhub.batstateu.edu.ph" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head reveal">
        <span class="sec-num">04</span>
        <div>
          <span class="sec-kicker">Selected projects</span>
          <h2>Things I've built</h2>
          <p>Filter by discipline – the mix runs from CRM automation through to machine learning.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="filter-bar reveal" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects by discipline">
        <button class="chip" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All <span class="count">4</span></button>
        <button class="chip" data-filter="automation" aria-pressed="false">Automation <span class="count">1</span></button>
        <button class="chip" data-filter="fullstack" aria-pressed="false">Full-stack <span class="count">2</span></button>
        <button class="chip" data-filter="frontend" aria-pressed="false">Front-end <span class="count">2</span></button>
        <button class="chip" data-filter="data" aria-pressed="false">Data &amp; AI <span class="count">2</span></button>
      </div>
      <p class="filter-status" id="filterStatus" role="status">Showing all 4 projects</p>

      <div class="projects" id="projectsGrid">
        <div class="project-card reveal" data-tags="automation">
          <span class="p-num">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Experience Vegas</h3>
            <span class="loc">Destination ticketing platform · USA</span>
            <ul>
              <li>Developed workflow automations that streamlined customer journeys.</li>
              <li>Managed weekly event listings and promotional content for Las Vegas events.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="project-tags"><span class="tag">GoHighLevel</span><span class="tag">Zapier</span><span class="tag">Ops</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card reveal" data-tags="fullstack data frontend">
          <span class="p-num">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Vision Drive</h3>
            <span class="loc">AI intelligent transport system · Philippines</span>
            <ul>
              <li>Built real-time analytics dashboards using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Firebase, and Chart.js.</li>
              <li>Developed live vehicle classification and traffic monitoring visualizations.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="project-tags"><span class="tag">JavaScript</span><span class="tag">Firebase</span><span class="tag">Chart.js</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card reveal" data-tags="data">
          <span class="p-num">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Hybrid Fraud Detection System</h3>
            <span class="loc">Capstone project · Philippines</span>
            <ul>
              <li>Developed a fraud detection framework using Python, statistical anomaly detection, and machine learning.</li>
              <li>Applied Z-score analysis and Benford's Law to flag suspicious patterns in insurance claim data.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="project-tags"><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">ML</span><span class="tag">Statistics</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card reveal" data-tags="fullstack frontend">
          <span class="p-num">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>University Public Dashboard</h3>
            <span class="loc">Research portal · Philippines</span>
            <ul>
              <li>Built a centralized research portal using Next.js, React.js, Node.js, and Tailwind CSS.</li>
              <li>Integrated APIs and advanced search for improved research accessibility.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="project-tags"><span class="tag">Next.js</span><span class="tag">React</span><span class="tag">Node.js</span><span class="tag">Tailwind</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
